 "text": "Hi, how you doing these days? She's trained you well. Cats learn quickly that a bit of body movement during a call gets their owner to stop and play. That's the training she's given you. I'm fine. Just tired. Long day at work. Lots of power outages. People panicking. They were scared, but manageable. It's the adults I feel for. That would mean a lot. I' text you when I' almost home. Sure thing. At the bit about your cat using your keyboard. She will. Cats are smarter than people give them credit for.",
